@baseUrl = http://localhost:5181
@landlordToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@landlordBToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@investorToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@adminToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@landId = <land-id-from-create>
@documentId = <document-id-from-upload>

# Security cases for step 4 (SEC-06, 07, 09, 11, 13, 14, 15, 17, 18).
# Result legend:
#   PASS           executed by a driver; the actual result matched the expectation
#   FAIL           executed; the actual result did not match
#   BLOCKED        not executed here. The admin cases in this file were BLOCKED until the
#                  approved C1 recovery (the placeholder SuperAdmin was removed and the app's
#                  own Development SuperAdminSeeder created a working account from Seed:*);
#                  the driver %TEMP%\opencode\s4_admin.ps1 then executed them: 39 PASS / 0 FAIL.
#   NOT VERIFIED   not executed in this remediation; no safe trigger exists here
# Code-review-only checks are labelled as such and are not counted as PASS.
# These requests were NOT sent through this file in an HTTP client. Each case was
# executed as an equivalent request by a PowerShell driver (s4_tests.ps1,
# s4_regression.ps1, s4_review.ps1, s4_review2.ps1 in %TEMP%\opencode) against the
# running app on localhost:5181.
# The admin cases (S4-50..S4-62) were BLOCKED until the approved C1 recovery. The driver
# s4_admin.ps1 (in %TEMP%\opencode) reads Seed:SuperAdminEmail/Password from user-secrets
# and never prints them; its first run returned 401 because NEBRASDB_Step1's sole SuperAdmin
# was the unauthenticatable model-seed placeholder (PASSWORD_HASH = 'N/A', no query filter,
# so the Development SuperAdminSeeder stayed a no-op while any RoleId=4 row existed). After
# the approved C1 change (placeholder removed; the app's own seeder created a working
# SuperAdmin from Seed:* on restart; normal login verified 200 and a SuperAdmin-gated call
# returned 200), the driver executed all 13 cases plus setup/verification checks:
# 39 PASS / 0 FAIL. Results per case are recorded on the case lines below.
# Post-remediation reruns: regression 47 PASS / 0 FAIL; full driver 51 PASS / 0 FAIL
# (the 13 admin cases previously reported BLOCKED were executed separately by
# s4_admin.ps1: 39 PASS / 0 FAIL); s4_review.ps1 (V-01..V-14) 14 PASS / 0 FAIL;
# s4_review2.ps1 (X-01..X-09) 9 PASS / 0 FAIL. Regression/V/X were rerun on fresh
# instances after the admin run and stayed green. Drivers are run on a fresh app:
# the auth endpoints are rate limited to 10 requests/minute per IP, so running them in
# the same minute as the other drivers yields 429 on login and empty tokens (401s).
# Never commit real tokens or passwords; replace the variables locally.

### SEC-13 filePath: http:// with a scheme — EXPECTED: 400
# Result: PASS (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/lands/{{landId}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{landlordToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "documentTypeId": 2, "filePath": "http://169.254.169.254/" }

### SEC-13 filePath: file:/// scheme — EXPECTED: 400
