# Result: PASS (200; driver S4-55)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/lands?status=PendingVerification
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### SEC-06: a v1-verified land keeps its criterion after a new criterion (S4-58)
# Result: PASS (DB unchanged; driver S4-58a). The land's VerifiedAgainstCriterionId
# does not change; a later criterion version is not applied retroactively.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/lands/{{landId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### SEC-14 admin-only: document-types DELETE of a used type — EXPECTED: 409 (S4-59)
# Result: PASS (409; driver S4-59b; an unused type is deleted 204 first — driver S4-59a)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/document-types/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

# ============================================================================
# Security re-review cases (V-01..V-14, X-01..X-09), rerun during remediation.
# Parallel and header cases cannot be expressed faithfully as single .http
# requests; each is executed by the driver named on the result line.
# ============================================================================

### SEC-15 headers on 404 / 201 / 401 — EXPECTED: exact CSP, nosniff, DENY, no-referrer
# Result: PASS 4/4 (V-01..V-04, rerun). Content-Security-Policy is exactly
# "default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'" on a 201, 401 and 404, with
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, X-Frame-Options: DENY, Referrer-Policy: no-referrer.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/lands/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{landlordToken}}

### SEC-09 visibility: missing resource vs another owner's resource
# Result: PASS (V-05 missing land -> 404; V-06 another landlord's land -> 403, rerun;
# and regression R-24..R-28 for lands, documents and eligibility). Convention: a
# missing/soft-deleted resource is 404, an existing resource the caller cannot access
# is 403. The 403 therefore reveals that the resource exists; this is accepted and is
# not described as concealment.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/lands/{{landId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{landlordBToken}}

### SEC-06/18 race: five parallel creates with the same parcel — EXPECTED: one 201, four 409, no 500
# Result: PASS (V-07..V-11, rerun; regression R-29..R-33). UQ_LAND_LOCATION is mapped to
# 409 like UQ_LAND_NUMBER_REGION; the response body exposes no SQL or index text, and the
# database holds exactly one live row. Driver: s4_review.ps1 / s4_regression.ps1.

### H1 race: concurrent document uploads must get distinct sequential versions
# Result: PASS (V-12..V-14 rerun: five parallel uploads -> five rows, versions 1..5;
# regression R-34.1..R-37: three rounds of five -> 15 rows, 15 distinct versions 1..15,
# no 500s). Driver: s4_review.ps1 / s4_regression.ps1.

### SEC-13/17: control characters in filePath — EXPECTED: 400
# Result: PASS (X-01 U+0001 -> 400; X-02 tab -> 400, rerun). FilePath keeps the strict
# NoControlCharacters rule; the free-text relaxation below does not apply to it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/lands/{{landId}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{landlordToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "documentTypeId": 2, "filePath": "docs/a\u0001b.pdf" }

### SEC-17: tab and newline are allowed in free text
# Result: PASS (X-03 newline and X-04 tab reach the service role check and return 403 for
# a landlord, rerun; regression R-38/R-39 reject, R-41 review note). The rule now allows
# U+0009 and U+000A and rejects the other U+0000..U+001F characters (X-05 U+0001 -> 400).
# Validation runs before the service role check, so a 403 proves the input was accepted.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/lands/{{landId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{landlordToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "line one\nline two" }

### SEC-07: protected fields on PUT are ignored; database confirmed unchanged
# Result: PASS (X-06 204; X-07 DB shows LAND_STATUS_ID=1, DATA_VERIFIED_BY_ADMIN=0,
# VERIFIED_AGAINST_CRITERION_ID=NULL after status/dataVerifiedByAdmin/
# verifiedAgainstCriterionId/landlordId were sent, rerun).
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/lands/{{landId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{landlordToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "regionId": 2, "gridId": 2, "landNumber": "L-<stamp>", "village": "Village-A", "basin": "Basin-A",
  "parcelNumber": "P-<stamp>", "areaDonum": 25, "slopePercentage": 5, "distanceToGridKm": 10,
  "solarIrradiance": 6, "elevationM": 100,
  "status": "Verified", "dataVerifiedByAdmin": true, "verifiedAgainstCriterionId": 999, "landlordId": 999999
}

### SEC-18: generic 500 body — EXPECTED: generic detail + traceId, no SQL/exception text
# Result: PASS (executed at runtime during this verification). A land create with
# areaDonum = 200,000,000 passed the old DTO bound but overflowed LANDS.AREA_DONUM
# decimal(10,2) in the database, and the handler returned exactly:
#   {"title":"An unexpected error occurred.","status":500,"detail":"An unexpected error
#    occurred.","errorCode":"INTERNAL_ERROR","traceId":"<correlation-id>"}
# with Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'. No SQL, stack
# trace or exception text was in the body; the SqlException text appeared only in the
# server log. That input now returns 400 (SEC-14 fix, driver R-43), so this trigger no
# longer exists; the duplicate-parcel race also yields zero 500s (X-08/X-09).
